// TEST: a reduction-join leg captured by another leg folds its snapshot (rejects)
// BORROW (2026-11-23): now refused at the write (BL4005, formalism 10.2): an uncomputed value
// over the written storage is still used after it. The text below is the schedule it witnessed (gap G233).
// Gap G233, round 4 wave 10: the join keeps the leg name p (written
// `reduce(p, (+))`) and the leg q's kernel captures p, so the prelude forces
// p under its own name; the C++ lane refused the join (BL7001, the stored
// leaf had no traversal) and the interpreter fell back. The p leg folds the
// stored snapshot through its stored-leaf traversal.
let mut x: Array<Float64 like Idx<2>> = [1.0, 2.0]
